course: dictionary
lesson: 1180
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words around them, tells you which meaning the writer means. «Grab the broom.» Here broom is something you hold, so it is a brush with a long handle.
explain: Now read this: «Gorse, broom and Himalayan balsam have pods that dry and twist on hot dry days until they burst.» Pods and seeds show that broom is a plant here, a wild bush. Always ask: which meaning fits the sentence? Then try it and check.
explain: Use the clues in the whole sentence. «By nine next morning half the street is there with brooms, a ladder and tea» shows people cleaning up after a problem, so broom means the cleaning tool.
fact: Broom (noun) means a brush with a long handle for sweeping floors.
fact: Broom also means a wild bush with small yellow flowers.
fact: Context clues tell you which meaning of a word the writer means.
fact: «A new broom sweeps clean» is a phrase meaning that a new leader makes many changes.
exercise: «Grab the broom.» What is a broom in this sentence? | A cup of tea | A wild bush with small yellow flowers | A ladder for reaching the window | *A brush with a long handle for sweeping
exercise: «Gorse, broom and Himalayan balsam have pods that dry and twist on hot dry days until they burst.» What kind of thing is broom in this sentence? | A brush for sweeping the floor | A type of bird that sings | *A wild bush with small yellow flowers | A kind of tea
exercise: The phrase «a new broom sweeps clean» means? | A new brush cleans very well | Sweeping is fun for everyone | *A new leader makes many changes | Leaves must be swept every day
test: «By nine next morning half the street is there with brooms, a ladder and tea.» What are the people using brooms for? | Growing yellow flowers | Flying to school | *Sweeping up and clearing mess | Balancing on their palms
test: In sport, curling players use brooms. What do they do with the brooms? | Sweep the leaves off the path | *Sweep the ice | Hang them on a wall | Plant them in the ground
exam: What does broom mean in «The Mole was spring-cleaning with brooms, dusters and a pail of whitewash»? | A white paint for walls | A pail for carrying water | A wild bush with small yellow flowers | *A brush with a long handle for sweeping
